  "query_preview": "(Thursday through Next Tuesday)...\nAs the front sags south of the area on Thursday, high pressure \nwill build across the Upper Midwest, gradually shifting eastward\ntoward the Great Lakes by Friday. This will usher in a much \ndrier and more seasonable air mass. Expect quiet, pleasant \nconditions across central Illinois by Friday with high \ntemperatures returning to seasonal norms in the 80s. Heading \ninto the weekend and early next week, the synoptic-scale pattern\nis projected to flatten into a low-amplitude, zonal flow \nregime. A series of weak, progressive waves will traverse this \nflow, introducing periodic chances for showers and \nthunderstorms. Due to persistent model discrepancies and low \npredictability inherent in these low-amplitude systems, a \nbroad-brushed 20-40% Probability of Precipitation (PoP) has been\nmaintained from Friday night through next Tuesday by the NBM.",
